{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And I will bless those who bless you.</b> Midrash Tanchuma: The Holy One, blessed be He, said to Abraham: From you will come forth a tribe that blesses the children — this is the tribe of Levi, from whom came forth priests who bless Israel. Abraham said to Him: And who blesses that tribe? He said to him: I will bless them, as it is written: ״ואני אברכם״. Thus it is written: ״ואברכה מברכיך״. And it seems to me this is what the Sages said in tractate חולין: the blessing of the priests — from where do we learn it? From ״אברכה מברכיך״." "<b>And all the families of the earth shall be blessed through you, etc.</b> When all the families intermingle, all will desire to join with you — and 'shall be blessed' (ונברכו) is in the sense of 'joining' (המבריך), as in grafting."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "Reading 'בני' in the midrash as 'the children' (of Israel); it may also be read as 'my sons.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:19.123011195Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}